 <h2 data-i18n="m13">The island in four parts</h2>
 <p data-i18n="m14">The north, around Nungwi and Kendwa, is the lively end: swimmable all day regardless of the tide, and busy with it. The east coast, Paje and Jambiani, is the kitesurfing coast, where the tide sets the rhythm of the day and the water walks a long way out. Stone Town sits on the west, an easy day out and a real one. The south, where the villa is, stays quiet &mdash; not because it is remote, but because nothing was ever built here at scale.</p>
